@page "/components/ai/emptystate"

<PageOutlet Url="components/ai/emptystate"
            Title="AiEmptyState"
            Description="BitAiEmptyState is what an empty AI conversation shows: a glyph, a heading, a line under it, and starter prompts the user can begin from with one tap." />

<DemoPage Name="AiEmptyState"
          Description="BitAiEmptyState is what an empty conversation shows: a glyph, a heading, a supporting line, and example prompts the user can start from with one tap. The suggestions matter more than the heading - an empty box is the hardest part of a chat product, and three concrete examples solve it. BitAiChat renders one until the first message; render it yourself in the EmptyTemplate of a BitAiMessageList."
          Parameters="componentParameters"
          SubClasses="componentSubClasses"
          CssVariables="componentCssVariables"
          GitHubAIUrl="EmptyState/BitAiEmptyState.razor"
          GitHubDemoUrl="AI/EmptyState/BitAiEmptyStateDemo.razor">
    <NotesTemplate>
        <BitText>
            To use this component, you need to install the
            <BitLink Href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/Bit.BlazorUI.AI" Target="_blank">
                <BitTag Reversed
                        Text="Bit.BlazorUI.AI"
                        Color="BitColor.SecondaryBackground"
                        IconName="@BitIconName.NavigateExternalInline" />
            </BitLink>
            nuget package, as described in the Optional steps of the
            <BitLink Href="/getting-started">Getting started</BitLink> page.
        </BitText>
        <br />
        <BitText>
            It needs no session: <b>OnSuggestion</b> hands the chosen prompt to the page, which submits it (a BitAiChat submits
            its own suggestions to its session). The heading and the line default to the EmptyTitle and EmptyBody strings of the
            <BitLink Href="/components/ai/optionsprovider">BitAiUiOptions</BitLink> in force, so a localized string table
            changes them everywhere. The glyph is decorative and hidden from assistive technologies; the suggestions are
            buttons, reachable with the keyboard. See the <BitLink Href="/ai/scenarios/basic">basic chat</BitLink> scenario.
        </BitText>
    </NotesTemplate>
    <Examples>
        <DemoExample Title="Basic" RazorCode="@example1RazorCode" Id="example1">
            <div>
                With nothing set, it greets with the words of the string table under a sparkle.
            </div>
            <br />
            <BitAiEmptyState />
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Title & body" RazorCode="@example2RazorCode" Id="example2">
            <div>
                <b>Title</b> and <b>Body</b> replace the words of the string table; <b>ChildContent</b> takes the place of the
                line with markup of your own.
            </div>
            <br />
            <BitAiEmptyState Title="Ask the docs assistant" Body="It knows every component of bit BlazorUI." />
            <br />
            <BitAiEmptyState Title="Start a new thread">
                Questions are answered from the <BitLink Href="/components">component gallery</BitLink> and nothing else.
            </BitAiEmptyState>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Suggestions" RazorCode="@example3RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example3CsharpCode" Id="example3">
            <div>
                <b>Suggestions</b> are offered as one-tap starters, and <b>OnSuggestion</b> hands the chosen one over - submit it
                to a session, as a BitAiChat does.
            </div>
            <br />
            <BitAiEmptyState Title="What can I help with?" Suggestions="suggestions" OnSuggestion="HandleSuggestion" />
            <br />
            <div>Chosen: <b>@(chosenSuggestion ?? "-")</b></div>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Icon" RazorCode="@example4RazorCode" Id="example4">
            <div>
                <b>IconName</b> picks another glyph of the built-in Fluent UI icons, and <b>IconTemplate</b> takes any markup in
                its place - a logo, an avatar, an emoji.
            </div>
            <br />
            <BitAiEmptyState IconName="@BitIconName.Robot" Title="Hi, I am Bit" />
            <br />
            <BitAiEmptyState Title="Welcome back">
                <IconTemplate>
                    <span style="font-size:2.5rem">👋</span>
                </IconTemplate>
            </BitAiEmptyState>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Disabled" RazorCode="@example5RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example5CsharpCode" Id="example5">
            <div>
                A disabled empty state disables its suggestions - while the chat around it cannot take a message, for instance.
            </div>
            <br />
            <BitAiEmptyState Disabled Title="The assistant is offline" Suggestions="suggestions" />
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Cascading parameters" RazorCode="@example6RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example6CsharpCode" Id="example6">
            <div>
                <b>BitParams</b> with a <b>BitAiEmptyStateParams</b> sets the words and the glyph every empty state inside it
                greets with - the one of each BitAiChat in it included; an empty state's own value wins (the second keeps its
                own title). The suggestions, the templates and the callback are not cascaded.
            </div>
            <br />
            <BitParams Parameters="emptyStateParams">
                <BitAiEmptyState />
                <br />
                <BitAiEmptyState Title="Its own title wins" />
            </BitParams>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="External Icons" RazorCode="@example7RazorCode" Id="example7">
            <div>
                <b>Icon</b> takes any CSS-class icon library (raw classes or <b>BitIconInfo.Css</b> / <b>Fa</b> / <b>Bi</b>) and
                wins over <b>IconName</b>. Reference the library's stylesheet in your app.
            </div>
            <br />
            <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/7.0.1/css/all.min.css" />
            <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/bootstrap-icons/1.11.3/font/bootstrap-icons.min.css" />
            <BitAiEmptyState Icon="@BitIconInfo.Fa("solid wand-magic-sparkles")" Title="FontAwesome" />
            <br />
            <BitAiEmptyState Icon="@BitIconInfo.Bi("chat-dots")" Title="Bootstrap Icons" />
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Style & Class" RazorCode="@example8RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example8CsharpCode" Id="example8">
            <div>
                <b>Style</b> / <b>Class</b> reach the root, <b>Styles</b> / <b>Classes</b> each part (the icon, the title, the
                body, the suggestions and each suggestion button, with the class-styles of BitButton). The public
                <b>--bit-AiEmptyState-*</b> variables (see the CSS variables table) re-skin it from <b>:root</b>, an ancestor
                or <b>Style</b>.
            </div>
            <br />
            <div>
                <BitAiEmptyState Title="Styled"
                                 Suggestions="suggestions"
                                 Style="border-radius:1rem;background:linear-gradient(180deg, var(--bit-clr-pri-tint), transparent)"
                                 Styles="@(new() { Title = "font-style:italic", Suggestion = new() { Root = "border-radius:0.25rem" } })" />
                <br />
                <BitAiEmptyState Title="Classy"
                                 Class="custom-empty"
                                 Classes="@(new() { Icon = "custom-empty-icon", Title = "custom-empty-title" })" />
                <br />
                <BitAiEmptyState Title="CSS variables"
                                 Suggestions="suggestions"
                                 Style="--bit-AiEmptyState-gap:0.5rem;--bit-AiEmptyState-padding:1.5rem;--bit-AiEmptyState-color:var(--bit-clr-fg-pri);--bit-AiEmptyState-icon-color:var(--bit-clr-suc);--bit-AiEmptyState-icon-size:4rem;--bit-AiEmptyState-title-color:var(--bit-clr-suc);--bit-AiEmptyState-title-font-size:2rem;--bit-AiEmptyState-title-font-weight:300;--bit-AiEmptyState-suggestions-gap:1rem" />
            </div>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="RTL" RazorCode="@example9RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example9CsharpCode" Id="example9">
            <div>Use BitAiEmptyState in right-to-left (RTL).</div>
            <br />
            <BitAiEmptyState Dir="BitDir.Rtl"
                             Title="چطور می‌توانم کمک کنم؟"
                             Body="پیامی بنویسید یا یکی از پیشنهادها را انتخاب کنید."
                             Suggestions="rtlSuggestions" />
        </DemoExample>
    </Examples>
</DemoPage>
